  "details": "Currently I have a gesture_lock bound to the right thumbpad south click, as well as using advanced template as a base. Naturally, soft gesture select works fine (trigger pull + gesture wheel select to bind that gesture to the trigger pull) until the following.\n\nWhen gesture_lock is invoked from that thumbpad click, soft gesture select activates permanently, constantly overriding the gesture bound to the trigger pull whenever the gesture wheel is activated, *despite trigger not being pulled*.\n\nThe main issue there is the fact that this bug is occurs inconsistently. I've narrowed it down to gesture lock action being involved 100% of the time (and specifically the controller action as of the most recent update), but it also seems like clicking the thumbpad and/or opening the quick menu on that controller has something to do with it. You have better debugging options, figure it out.",
